[Music]  hey guys it's Jonah here who loves to  eat rice  hey I'm Asian of course I love rice rice  is so easy to cook it is versatile and  you know what rice can be very healthy  so I'm gonna share with you three rice  recipes which you can prep ahead and it  is perfect for your family dinner let's  start with a really simple recipe while  rice and bean salad so this recipe is  great as a starter or even as a main  meal so what I've used are one cup of  cooked and chilled wild rice you can use  any other rice of your choice have a can  of beans rinsed and drinked again choose  any beans of your choice half a red bell  pepper diced 1/2 a cup of cherry  tomatoes haft 1 small onion diced  quarter cup of corn quarter cup of  cucumber diced cut a cup of olives as  for the dressing you'll need 3  tablespoons of lemon juice 1 tablespoon  of olive oil 1/2 a teaspoon of maple  syrup 1/2 a teaspoon of smoked paprika  quarter teaspoon of cumin powder quarter  teaspoon of garlic powder and salt and  black pepper to taste in a small bowl  mix together all the dressing  ingredients and set aside to make the  salad all you have to do is assemble all  the ingredients in a bowl so let's start  with the rice as the base and all the  vegetables beans bell pepper cucumber  corn cherry tomatoes onion and olives  drizzle with a little bit of dressing  and serve it really is that simple when  you want to eat it simply toss all the  ingredients together this dish is so  colorful its nutritious and it is  absolutely delicious so this one huge  bowl of rice salad has about 305  calories plus it provides you with your  3 a day this dish is also great to be  eaten chilled so you can prep 3 to 4  servings and just  keep it in the fridge separate the  dressing to keep your salad fresh okay  I'm really excited about this next  recipe  I can't stop making it for dinner yep it  is the one pot fish and rice soup I love  soup and it goes perfectly with rice for  this recipe what you'll need are four  cups of broth chicken fish or vegetable  about 400 gram of Dori fish fillet or  any other fish fillet of your choice  half a cup of uncooked rice rinsed have  a can of beans rinsed and drained have a  can of diced tomatoes 1 teaspoon of  cumin powder one teaspoon of garlic  powder one teaspoon of cayenne pepper  one teaspoon of mixed herbs and one  teaspoon of salt  we want to start by prepping the rice so  feel a large pot with four cups of broth  and the uncooked rice cover bring to a  boil and allow the rice to almost cook  for about 25 to 30 minutes so you want  to adjust the cooking time depending on  the rice you're using once the rice is  almost ready let's stir in all the  ingredients fish beans diced tomatoes  corn and all the spices allow all the  ingredients to simmer for another 10 to  15 minutes until the fish and rice are  fully cooked and the soup thickens  slightly don't forget to stir  occasionally serve hot I love this  recipe because it is so versatile you  can simply change the ingredients  according to what's available  this dish is also very high in protein  so it is a great post-workout meal one  serving has about 360 calories and 28  grams of protein plus soups fill you up  very quickly so it is a great dish if  you're watching your waist line  you know what I love it when I can use  the same recipe change it a little bit  and create a whole new dish so for my  final recipe we're going to use what we  have cooked and create stuffed bell  pepper rice here's what we're going to  do preheat the oven to 180 degrees  Celsius let's start by prepping the bell  peppers cut the top part of the bell  peppers and scoop up the seeds to create  a pocket we want to feel each bell  pepper with the rice mixture from the  previous recipe fill them up without at  the soup and set aside next fill up the  bottom of a baking dish with thickly  sliced potato and carrots you want to  keep them as leveled and flat as  possible then place the stuffed bell  peppers 